meta {
  name: contact
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/public/contact/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    // Required.
    "name": "Julia Brandt",

    // Required.
    "email": "traveller@example.com",

    // Optional, defaults to "other". The contact page's subject dropdown.
    // One of: "online_classes", "immersion", "homestay", "travel_spanish", "other".
    // Fetch the labels from GET /public/contact/subjects/.
    "subject": "immersion",

    // Required.
    "message": "Hello! I am travelling to Ecuador in November and would like to know if the Quito Immersion Program has space.",

    // Optional free text. Set it when the enquiry came from a specific
    // Study-in-Quito programme page, e.g. "Quito Immersion Program".
    "programme": "Quito Immersion Program"
  }
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  Contact form and the "Inquire about a programme" CTA. Stores the message,
  acknowledges it to the sender and notifies `SCHOOL_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL`.

  Immersion programmes are coordinated by hand -- this is an enquiry, not a
  checkout.

  The 48-hour promise in the acknowledgement email comes from
  `public.views.RESPONSE_TIME_HOURS`. That figure is still unconfirmed with the
  school (open item A4); change it in one place if they say 24.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Thanks -- we'll reply within 48 hours, Monday to Friday.",
    "id": "b3d91f47-2c8a-4e15-9f60-7a2d1e4c8b93"
  }
}
